  "id": "premorbid-abilities",
  "term": "premorbid abilities",
  "definition": "Premorbid abilities are a person’s cognitive abilities as they were before the onset of neurological or cognitive impairment. In neuropsychological assessment, they are estimated indirectly from test scores on functions that tend to stay relatively preserved, often using so-called hold tests such as word-reading tasks.",
